<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khmu people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khmu are an Austroasiatic-speaking people of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> and neighbouring parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Regarded as among the earliest inhabitants of the region, they were long subordinate to the Lao kingdoms, and they had a ritual role at the royal court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luang-prabang">Luang Prabang</a> acknowledging their status as first inhabitants. They are the largest upland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lao-theung">Lao Theung</a> group in Laos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khmu-people.jpg" alt="Khmu people" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tango7174 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bokeo_BanHuayHao4_tango7174.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
